#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# principal_components

#% text
# `principal_components(data)` gives the rows of the numeric matrix `data` in the coordinates of the principal axes, the eigenvectors of the covariance matrix.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The columns of the result are ordered by decreasing variance; the mean of each column is subtracted first.

#% item
# The sign of each axis is fixed by making the first component of the axis negative.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
principal_components([[1., 2.], [2., 3.], [4., 10.]])
#% output
#= [[3.2705329110195445, 0.28529328017989053], [1.9996938973384735, -0.3351647774727787], [-5.270226808358019, 0.04987149729288731]]

#% cell
covariance(principal_components([[1., 2.], [2., 3.], [4., 10.]]))
#% output
#= [[21.23522590832513, -1.1102230246251565e-16], [-1.1102230246251565e-16, 0.09810742500820661]]

